{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011Cf5jNT2J5ujqjfVT6mRRZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect. Now I have a clear picture of the codebase. Let me summarize the analysis:\n\n**Repository findings:**\n- `ShipmentController.kt:20-56` — defines POST/GET endpoints\n- `Shipment.kt:9-27` — model with `ShipmentStatus` enum (CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED)\n- `ShipmentRepository.kt` — in-memory storage with `save()` and `findById()` methods\n- `ApiExceptions.kt:19-24` — `ResourceNotFoundException` (404) and `ConflictException` (409)\n- `ApiError.kt:31-37` — `ErrorCode` enum currently has SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS\n- `GlobalExceptionHandler.kt` — centralizes error handling by status code\n- `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — uses MockMvc; tests check status codes and error codes\n\n**Conventions:**\n1. Throw `ResourceNotFoundException` for 404 (resource not found)\n2. Throw `ConflictException` for 409 (state conflict)\n3. Success responses wrap in `ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.CREATED)`\n4. GET operations return raw resource (not wrapped)\n5. Error codes are members of `ErrorCode` enum\n6. Tests use `post()` builders and check `jsonPath()` for both success and error fields\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `ApiError.kt` — must add error code for \"cannot confirm cancelled shipment\"\n2. `ShipmentController.kt` — must add `confirm` endpoint\n3. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — must add tests for confirm behavior\n\n**Risks:**\n- Breaking existing tests if confirm logic interferes with existing operations\n- Not persisting the state change properly\n- Missing idempotency case (repeated confirms must succeed)\n\n**Open questions:** None — the ticket fully specifies the behavior.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed changes:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** — Add `SHIPMENT_CANCELLED` to `ErrorCode` enum. This covers the case where confirming a cancelled shipment is rejected.\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** — Add a new endpoint `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm`:\n   - Retrieve shipment by ID; throw `ResourceNotFoundException` if not found (404)\n   - If status is `CANCELLED`, throw `ConflictException` with `SHIPMENT_CANCELLED` code (409)\n   - If status is `CREATED`, update it to `CONFIRMED` and save\n   - If status is already `CONFIRMED`, do nothing (idempotency — succeeds, no change)\n   - Return the shipment with HTTP 200\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Add four tests:\n   - Test confirming a `CREATED` shipment transitions it to `CONFIRMED`\n   - Test confirming an already `CONFIRMED` shipment succeeds without changing it (idempotency)\n   - Test confirming a `CANCELLED` shipment returns 409 with `SHIPMENT_CANCELLED` code\n   - Test confirming a nonexistent shipment returns 404 with `SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND` code\n\n**Alternatives considered and rejected:**\n- Using a separate service layer: The existing code doesn't have one; all logic is in the controller. Staying consistent is simpler.\n- Making confirm a PATCH instead of POST: The ticket explicitly says `POST`, so that's not an option.\n- Adding a generic \"INVALID_STATE\" error code: `SHIPMENT_CANCELLED` is more specific and follows the existing pattern (SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS).\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\nFor each case the ticket names:\n\n| Case | Input | Action | Output | Status |\n|------|-------|--------|--------|--------|\n| Confirm CREATED | GET by ID → CREATED | update status to CONFIRMED, save | Shipment(status=CONFIRMED) | 200 |\n| Confirm CONFIRMED (retry) | GET by ID → CONFIRMED | no change | Shipment(status=CONFIRMED) | 200 |\n| Confirm CANCELLED | GET by ID → CANCELLED | throw ConflictException | ApiError(SHIPMENT_CANCELLED) | 409 |\n| Confirm missing | GET by ID → null | throw ResourceNotFoundException | ApiError(SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND) | 404 |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\nEach test creates one or more shipments, calls confirm, and asserts on status and response:\n- **Test 1 (confirm-created):** Create S-1 in CREATED, confirm it, assert status=CONFIRMED and 200\n- **Test 2 (confirm-already-confirmed):** Create S-2 in CREATED, confirm twice, both succeed with 200, status stays CONFIRMED\n- **Test 3 (confirm-cancelled):** Create S-3 in CREATED, manually save it as CANCELLED (via direct repo write), confirm, expect 409 and error code\n- **Test 4 (confirm-missing):** Confirm nonexistent S-missing, expect 404 and error code\n\nNow I can proceed to implementation.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nLet me start by adding the error code:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1867,"cache_read_input_tokens":16724,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1867},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"587d3099-85f6-42ff-98a9-48590d5173cd","uuid":"d3128a9f-f0e0-4c75-bde1-b9c87f7edb08","timestamp":"2026-09-15T18:53:40.585Z","request_id":"req_011Cf5jNSH97SJQ5X9pVvkKN"}
